supuestos cerrados o fechas específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 102 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 17.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.4 to 8.0. December accounts for 4% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 61 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,446 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Statistical trends alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts awarded in December to see if they align with the body’s needs. Review the types of services provided by awardee A to determine if multiple contracts served the same purpose. Verify if contracts [1][2][3] were part of a larger procurement plan for the same service.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["eCSVELAXPQz%2Fa9DgO%2BoYKQ%3D%3D","fXb2CqzWcgiIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D","%2BX%2BdIJHHmvSHCIsjvJ3rhQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}